  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, config_006) achieves 0.653 acc, but adding resnet50 image features via concat fusion (config_030) drops performance to 0.632. This is surprising and suggests either the fusion strategy or the weak image signal (image_only resnet50 was only 0.208) is the bottleneck. Question: config_031 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding all other factors (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool) identical to config_030. This isolates whether the performance drop is due to the fusion mechanism (concat giving equal weight to a weak image signal) or the image representation itself. Why best: It is a single-variable, directly controlled comparison against config_030, making the result maximally interpretable. If weighted fusion recovers to ~0.65+, the issue is fusion strategy and we can exploit multimodal with resnet50. If it remains ~0.63, the image encoder is the bottleneck and the next experiment should test imagenet_vit_l. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about which design axis to pursue next, making this the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a limited budget."
}

